const lT = [{ group: "agreement", title: "The agreement and what it costs", blurb: "Services, rates, invoicing and cancellation. The part families ask about later." }, { group: "consent_to_care", title: "Consent to care", blurb: "Permission to treat, and confirmation they have the folder in their hands." }, { group: "permissions", title: "Optional permissions", blurb: "Photographs and transport. Both can be refused without affecting care \u2014 say so first." }, { group: "records", title: "Records and privacy", blurb: "Who may send us records, who we may send them to, and who we may talk to." }, { group: "rights", title: "Rights, complaints and emergencies", blurb: "Their rights, how to complain about us, and what to do in a storm or an emergency." }], Aa = [{ key: "services_and_schedule", title: "What we will do, and how often", pages: "1, 3", group: "agreement", say: "Read back the services, the days and the weekly hours. If anything is wrong, fix it now \u2014 they should not sign a schedule they did not agree to.", watchFor: "People hear the hours as a maximum. They are a commitment. Say the weekly total out loud.", mark: "signature", mandatory: true, fullText: "ACKNOWLEDGEMENT AND AGREEMENT: I, the undersigned, hereby make the following acknowledgement and agreements regarding services to be provided by Joy Healthcare Services, LLC. I agree to enter into an agreement for the following services. Joy Healthcare Services, LLC. agrees to provide the following services: Personal Care, Respite, Companionship, Light Housekeeping and other non-skilled services, at the stated frequency (SN frequency, CNA/HHA frequency, aide/sitter frequency), on the days marked M/T/W/TH/F/SA/SU, with the stated start time, end time and total weekly hours, from the start date to the end date or until services are no longer needed." }, { key: "fee_for_service", title: "The rates, and that they were sent to you", pages: "2, 4", group: "agreement", say: "Confirm they received the rates by e-mail. The rates are not in this packet on purpose \u2014 they go by e-mail for financial privacy.", watchFor: "Three rates, not one: the hourly rate, the 24/7 rate, and the RN assessment or visit rate. If they are only expecting an hourly figure, say all three now.", mark: "initials", mandatory: true, fullText: "FEE FOR SERVICE(S): I confirm that a representative from Joy Healthcare Services, LLC. has confirmed and reviewed the applicable service rates with me. These agreed-upon rate(s) have been documented, confirmed, and e-mailed to me to ensure financial privacy. I understand and accept the rates associated with the services requested. Joy Healthcare Services, LLC. rates for services are listed separately and the agreed upon rate(s) is/are stated there: HOURLY $____, 24/7 $____, RN ASSESSMENT/VISIT $____." }, { key: "deposit", title: "The deposit", pages: "2", group: "agreement", say: "One week of the agreed services, taken before care starts, and it is applied to the LAST week of service.", watchFor: "The old agreement applied the deposit to the FIRST weeks. This one applies it to the last. If they have seen an older copy, say the change out loud.", mark: "initials", mandatory: true, fullText: "DEPOSIT: A deposit equal to one week of the agreed-upon scheduled services is required prior to the start of care. The deposit will be applied toward the last week of service." }, { key: "holiday_overtime", title: "Holiday and overtime rates", pages: "2", group: "agreement", say: "Time and a half over 40 hours in a week for any one caregiver, and on seven named holidays.", watchFor: "Overtime is per caregiver. Two caregivers doing 30 hours each is not overtime, and families ask. Name the holidays if they are scheduling around one: New Year's Day, Memorial Day, Easter Sunday, Independence Day, Labor Day, Thanksgiving, Christmas.", mark: "initials", mandatory: true, fullText: "HOLIDAY/OVERTIME PAY: Joy Healthcare Services, LLC bills 1.5 times the applicable hourly rate when an individual caregiver works over 40 hours in a workweek or for services provided on designated holidays. Overtime is based on each caregiver's individual hours and is not calculated by combining hours worked by multiple caregivers. Holiday rates apply to services provided on: New Year's Day, Memorial Day, Easter Sunday, Independence Day, Labor Day, Thanksgiving Day, and Christmas Day." }, { key: "invoicing", title: "Invoicing and when payment is due", pages: "2", group: "agreement", say: "Invoiced weekly in advance, payment due within three calendar days. Say the numbers: 2.9% on credit cards, $5 on ACH, $100 late fee after the third day.", watchFor: "Say plainly that services can be suspended within 24 hours for non-payment \u2014 that part is real and it happens. Take the invoice e-mail address now; the invoice goes there, not to whoever happens to answer the phone.", mark: "initials", mandatory: true, fullText: "INVOICING FOR SERVICE(S): I understand that Joy Healthcare Services, LLC invoices weekly in advance. Due to billing in advance, the undersigned agrees to submit payment within 3 calendar days of the invoice date by credit card, debit card, automatic payment, or ACH. The undersigned will be legally responsible for all collection activity fees; legal fees incurred by Joy Healthcare Services, LLC. for collecting on delinquent invoices/monies owed to Joy Healthcare Services, LLC. Joy Healthcare Services, LLC applies a 2.9% convenience fee to all credit card payments and a $5 convenience fee to ACH debit payments. A fee will also apply to any outstanding invoice not paid in full within three (3) business days. Services may be suspended within 24 hours of non-payment. A late fee will incur after the third day of an outstanding invoice of $100. If a third party is utilized for payment of services, it is still the sole responsibility of the undersigned to ensure Joy Healthcare Services, LLC. receives payment on-time. Invoices should be e-mailed to the client/responsible party for payment at the e-mail address given." }, { key: "technology_setup_fee", title: "The one-time setup fee", pages: "2", group: "agreement", say: "One hundred dollars, once, on the first invoice \u2014 it sets up scheduling, documentation and the family's access.", watchFor: "It appears on the first invoice alongside the first week in advance and the deposit. Three charges at once surprises people. Say the total they should expect to see.", mark: "initials", mandatory: true, fullText: "TECHNOLOGY SETUP FEE: A one-time $100 technology setup fee will be billed on the initial invoice for the setup and activation of systems required to support scheduling, documentation, communication, and care coordination." }, { key: "changes_to_care", title: "Changing the care we agreed", pages: "3", group: "agreement", say: "Tell us as soon as anything needs to change. We write an addendum, you get an updated care plan, and the caregiver is told.", watchFor: "Also states that services are supervised annually or as needed \u2014 that is a visit they should expect, not an inspection they have done something to deserve.", mark: "initials", mandatory: true, fullText: "CHANGES TO POLICY: I confirm that I will notify the agency timely if I need to make any changes to the care identified in this agreement. If changes are requested to this agreement, a representative from Joy Healthcare Services, LLC. will contact me and an addendum will be added. In addition, I understand that I will receive an updated customized care plan and my caregiver will be notified of the changes. I understand that all services will be supervised by Joy Healthcare Services, LLC annually or as needed." }, { key: "cancellation", title: "Cancelling a visit, and ending care", pages: "3", group: "agreement", say: "Four numbers. They can stop at any time and only pay for care already given. Seven days' notice to end services and get the unused deposit back. Forty-eight hours to move or cancel a visit. Under 24 hours \u2014 or turning the caregiver away at the door \u2014 may be charged in full.", watchFor: "The last one is the argument. Say it now, in the room, rather than defending an invoice later: a caregiver who has already driven out gets paid.", mark: "signature", mandatory: true, fullText: "CANCELLATION OF POLICY: The client may cancel this agreement at any time and will only be charged for services already provided. A minimum of 7 days' notice is required to discontinue services and receive a refund of any unused deposit, less any outstanding balance. For individual scheduled visits, a minimum of 48 hours' notice is required to cancel or reschedule. Cancellations with less than 24 hours' notice, or services declined after a caregiver arrives, may be charged in full." }, { key: "payment_method", title: "How you will pay", pages: "4", group: "agreement", say: "Debit card, credit card or ACH. Pick one now \u2014 this is the electronic payment preference and it needs their signature.", watchFor: "The card fee follows the choice: 2.9% on a card, $5 on ACH. If they are paying weekly, that difference adds up and they may want to know it before choosing.", mark: "signature", mandatory: true, fullText: "ELECTRONIC PAYMENT PREFERENCE: Debit Card / Credit Card / ACH. ACKNOWLEDGMENT OF TERMS: I confirm that a representative from Joy Healthcare Services, LLC. has confirmed and reviewed the service rates, billing timeframe, invoicing, overtime/holiday pay, deposit, cancellation/change in service policy. These terms have been documented and provided to me in writing for my records. The agreed-upon rate(s) have been documented, confirmed, and e-mailed to me to ensure financial privacy. I agree with the terms of service." }, { key: "informed_consent_care", title: "What home care is, and what it is not", pages: "5", group: "agreement", say: "This is non-skilled care. The goal is to keep them safe, independent and at home for as long as it is right for them.", watchFor: "Two things people get wrong. Medication reminders are not medication administration. And no physician's order is needed for home care \u2014 families who have just come from a hospital often assume one is, and wait for it.", mark: "signature", mandatory: true, fullText: "INFORMED CONSENT FOR HOME CARE SERVICES. HOME CARE PHILOSOPHY/PURPOSE: I understand that Joy Healthcare provides non-skilled care. I understand the goal of Home care is to help with recovery, regain independence, become more self-sufficient, maintain current condition or level of function, and/or slow decline. I understand that the goal of Home Care is to support my safety, independence, comfort, and ability to remain in my preferred living environment for as long as appropriate. CRITERIA: I understand that Home Care services are based on an individualized assessment of my needs and do not require a physician's order. A representative of Joy Healthcare will review my care needs and develop a personalized plan of care based on the services requested and agreed upon. I understand that if my care needs change or exceed the services Joy Healthcare is able to provide, my plan of care may be updated, additional services may be recommended, or I may be referred to another provider. HOME CARE SERVICES: I understand that Joy Healthcare services are primarily provided in the home but may also be provided in other approved settings as appropriate. Services may include, but are not limited to, personal care, bathing, grooming, dressing, toileting, mobility assistance, meal preparation, light housekeeping, companionship, medication reminders, transportation assistance, and other authorized non-medical support services outlined in my plan of care. These services are individualized according to my needs and may be modified as those needs change. RESPITE CARE: Respite Care is provided to give a primary caregiver temporary relief and may be scheduled for an agreed-upon period of time. Respite services must be coordinated and authorized by the Joy Health Interdisciplinary Team. CONTINUOUS CARE: Continuous Care is provided in the home when a client requires more than 12 hours of care per day, up to 24 hours within a midnight-to-midnight period. Services are provided by authorized Joy Healthcare personnel and must be coordinated and approved in advance by the Joy Health Interdisciplinary Team." }, { key: "equipment_supplies_payment", title: "Equipment, supplies and who is responsible for paying", pages: "6", group: "agreement", say: "We do not supply equipment. You provide gloves and basic supplies; if they run out we will bring them and bill you.", watchFor: "The insurance sentence matters more than the supplies one. If they are counting on long-term care insurance, say it plainly: reimbursement is not guaranteed and they owe us either way.", mark: "initials", mandatory: true, fullText: "EQUIPMENT/SUPPLIES: I understand that Joy Healthcare does not provide durable medical equipment. I am responsible for obtaining and maintaining any equipment needed for my care. I also agree to provide essential caregiver supplies, including PPE, gloves, and other basic care items. If these supplies are not available, Joy Healthcare may provide them as needed, and the associated cost will be billed to me. AUTHORIZATION FOR PAYMENT: I understand that Joy Healthcare Services, LLC provides private-pay Home Care services and that I am responsible for payment in accordance with the agreed-upon rates, billing terms, and service agreement. If I use long-term care insurance or any other third-party benefit, I understand that reimbursement is not guaranteed. I remain fully responsible for all charges owed to Joy Healthcare Services, LLC, regardless of whether my insurance carrier reimburses me, delays payment, or denies coverage. I authorize Joy Healthcare to process payments using my approved method of payment for services rendered and other authorized charges." }, { key: "choice_of_care", title: "Stopping our care and going elsewhere", pages: "6", group: "agreement", say: "They can choose different care at any time \u2014 but it has to be in writing, and they have to tell us straight away.", watchFor: "Read the consequence out loud. If they stop using us without signing a revocation, they can be held responsible for ambulance, emergency room, hospital, treatment and physician costs. Nobody should meet that sentence for the first time in a dispute.", mark: "initials", mandatory: true, fullText: "CHOICE OF CARE: I understand that I may choose care other than the care that Joy Healthcare provides at any time by signing a revocation statement. I will notify Joy Health immediately of a decision to revoke home care services. Such a choice will automatically relieve Joy Health of any further responsibility of providing care to me. I understand that if I fail to sign a revocation statement and to notify Joy Healthcare in a timely manner, I may be held responsible for any and all charges incurred such as ambulance costs, emergency room or hospital cost, procedure/treatment costs, and/or physician costs." }, { key: "role_of_caregiver", title: "What the caregiver is not there to do", pages: "6", group: "agreement", say: "The caregiver supports them. They do not replace the family \u2014 appointments, emergencies and the things outside the care plan still need you.", watchFor: "Families arranging care from another state need this said kindly and clearly. Better now than during the first emergency.", mark: "initials", mandatory: true, fullText: "ROLE OF CAREGIVER IN HOME: I understand that Joy Healthcare caregivers are present to support the client and are not intended to replace the role of family members or other responsible parties. Family involvement may still be necessary for care needs, appointments, emergencies, and other responsibilities outside the caregiver's authorized duties." }, { key: "consent_for_care", title: "Consent for care, the client folder and release of information", pages: "7", group: "consent_to_care", say: "The consent to treat itself. Also confirms they have the admission folder, the privacy notice and the bill of rights in their hands.", watchFor: "States the cover hours: clinical staff Monday to Friday, 8 to 5, with an on-call line 24/7 for non-clinical questions.", mark: "initials", mandatory: true, fullText: "CONSENT FOR CARE: I hereby consent to the care provided by Joy Healthcare and authorize its agents and associates to provide care and treatment to me in my residence or facility according to program policy and as prescribed by my doctor, other healthcare provider(s), and/or Joy Healthcare's interdisciplinary team. I have been instructed by my doctor, other healthcare provider(s), and/or Joy Healthcare's interdisciplinary team about the prescribed treatment and understand the reasons it is considered necessary, along with its risks, advantages, possible complications, and alternatives. A representative of Joy Healthcare has explained the services and adequately answered all my questions. I understand that the goal of Home Health is to treat an illness or injury, while the goal of Homecare is to aid in recovery, regain independence, become more self-sufficient, maintain my current condition or level of function, and/or slow decline. I understand that clinical staff and nurses are available Monday through Friday, 8 AM to 5 PM, and that an on-call representative is available 24/7 to answer non-clinical questions. I agree to notify Joy Healthcare of any significant changes or concerns related to my health. I understand that I may refuse treatment or terminate services at any time, and that Joy Healthcare may terminate their services to me as explained in my orientation. ACKNOWLEDGEMENT OF CLIENT FOLDER: I acknowledge receipt of the Client Admission Folder, including the Notice of Privacy Practices and Bill of Rights, and confirm my understanding and agreement with its contents. My signature on the consents indicates my approval and receipt of the Client Admission Folder. RELEASE OF INFORMATION/PRIVACY LAW: I acknowledge receipt of the Notice of Privacy Practices and was given the opportunity to ask questions and voice concerns. I have received a copy of the Joy Healthcare Notice of Privacy Practices, which describes how my medical information may be disclosed and how I may access this information. I understand that the company may use or disclose protected health information about me to carry out treatment, obtain payment, or conduct healthcare-related operations. I hereby authorize Joy Healthcare to release to or receive from hospitals, physicians, or other agencies involved in my case all medical records and information pertinent to my care. I also give permission for my medical record to be reviewed by accrediting agencies and/or other regulatory bodies. ACCESS INFORMATION: I have completed the Permission to Disclose Protected Health Information Form and understand that only those names whom I have listed may communicate with Joy Healthcare staff regarding my healthcare. This information is maintained by Joy Health and subject to applicable laws and agency policies." }, { key: "customer_rights", title: "Rights, safety, after hours and filming for our records", pages: "8", group: "consent_to_care", say: "Their rights and responsibilities, what to do after hours, and who we bill. Confirm they know to call 911 first for a medical emergency.", watchFor: "This page carries its own consent to film or record for internal and insurance documentation \u2014 separate from the photograph consent on page 10. If they refuse photographs, say so here too and note it. Billing is Self-Pay or Long Term Care Insurance; there is no Medicare or Medicaid option on this packet.", mark: "initials", mandatory: true, fullText: "CUSTOMER RIGHTS/RESPONSIBILITIES: I have received a copy and an explanation of the Patient Bill Of Rights and Responsibilities. I acknowledge that I have been made aware of my rights and responsibilities as a customer and I understand them. I understand I have the right to choose my health care provider/agency, and I choose Joy Healthcare for my home care services. SAFETY/COMPLAINTS: I have received information regarding safety issues that I may encounter during my illness. I understand that Joy Healthcare will respond to my concerns. Grievance and Complaint procedures have been explained to me. Additionally, the purpose and hours of operation of the state hotline have been provided and explained to me. Joy Healthcare Services, LLC. and its employees are mandated reporters of suspected abuse and will report concerns as required by Texas state law. EDUCATIONAL MATERIAL: I acknowledge receipt of educational materials and have been given an explanation of all services, equipment, and supplies. A home safety assessment was conducted during the admission process and applicable safety precautions material was given to me. AFTER HOURS/EMERGENCY INFORMATION: I understand for medical emergencies to call 9-1-1. I have been informed on how and when to contact Joy Healthcare in the event of an emergency or after hours. ADVANCE DIRECTIVES: I have received an explanation and written information regarding Texas Advance Directives. I understand that the Federal Patient Self-Determination Act of 1990 requires that I be made aware of my right to make healthcare decisions for myself. I understand that I can express my wishes in a document titled an Advance Directive. CONSENT TO FILM/RECORD: I hereby consent for Joy Healthcare to record or film my care, treatment and services and allow Joy Healthcare to use the photographs/recordings for their internal use, for documenting my medical condition or for insurance providers to document my condition for payment purposes. LIABILITY/ASSIGNMENT OF PAYMENT: I further understand services provided by Joy Healthcare will be billed out to: Self-Pay or Long Term Care Insurance." }, { key: "complaints", title: "How to complain about us", pages: "8, 9", group: "rights", say: "Give them the number: 713 231 9662, staffed 24 hours. Then give them the state hotline too \u2014 they are entitled to go over our heads.", watchFor: "Do not skip the HHSC contact, and say its hours. Offering it builds more trust than withholding it. A complaint can be filed by mail, fax, e-mail or the OCR Complaint Portal.", mark: "initials", mandatory: true, fullText: "SAFETY/COMPLAINTS: Grievance and Complaint procedures have been explained to me. Additionally, the purpose and hours of operation of the state hotline have been provided and explained to me. I have been notified of my right to voice a complaint and understand that I may first file a complaint with the Agency Administrator or designee at the above referenced phone number. I can also contact the State Hotline in the event that I need information or if I have a complaint. This includes a complaint regarding advance directives. The complaint must be filed in writing by mail, fax, e-mail, or via the OCR Complaint Portal. Joy Healthcare: 713 231 9662, a staff member is available 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. HHSC Complaint and Incident Intake, Mail Code E249, P.O. Box 149030, Austin, Texas 78714-9030. Toll Free: 1-800-458-9858 (7AM-7PM Mon-Fri). crscomplaints@hhscdads.state.tx.us." }, { key: "advance_directive", title: "Advance directives", pages: "8, 9", group: "rights", say: "Explain what an advance directive is, and say clearly that they do not need one to receive care.", watchFor: "It is unlawful to require one. If they do not have one, that is a complete answer \u2014 record it and move on.", mark: "initials", mandatory: false, allowNotApplicable: true, fullText: "ADVANCE DIRECTIVES: I have received an explanation and written information regarding Texas Advance Directives. I understand that the Federal Patient Self-Determination Act of 1990 requires that I be made aware of my right to make healthcare decisions for myself. I understand that I can express my wishes in a document titled an Advance Directive. Under these laws, it is unlawful for any person or organization to require an individual to execute advance directives as a condition for receiving services or care. An individual is not required to have an advance directive in order to receive home care services." }, { key: "documents_reviewed", title: "Everything we went through today", pages: "9", group: "consent_to_care", say: "The checklist of what was reviewed before care starts. Read it as a list \u2014 it is the page a surveyor turns to first.", watchFor: "Only sign this once the items above it are genuinely done. It asserts the folder, the rights, the transfer and discharge policy and the complaint route were all explained. The printed list still carries an OASIS line, which belongs to home health rather than home care \u2014 flag it for the next reprint rather than reading it as a home care obligation.", mark: "signature", mandatory: true, fullText: "A representative from Joy Healthcare has reviewed the following documents prior to the start of home care services: I have been informed in a language and agree to the Authorization To Obtain & Release Medical Records. I have been informed and agree to the Patient/Client Service Agreement. I have been informed and agree to the Informed Consent for Home care Services. I have received a copy and an explanation of my Patient Rights and Responsibilities. I have received a copy and an explanation of the Agency's transfer and discharge policies. I have received a copy and an explanation of Solicitation. I have been informed of my rights in a language and manner that I understand. I have received and understand the contact information including the names, addresses, and telephone numbers of the Agency Administrator, Clinical Managers(s), and Federal/State funded entities that serve the area where I reside. I have been notified of my right to voice a complaint and understand that I may first file a complaint with the Agency Administrator or designee at the above referenced phone number. I can also contact the State Hotline in the event that I need information or if I have a complaint. This includes a complaint regarding advance directives. The complaint must be filed in writing by mail, fax, e-mail, or via the OCR Complaint Portal. I have received information on Advance Directives. I understand that it is in my right and responsibility to be involved in my care and that I will be informed as to the nature and purpose of any technical procedure. I have received and reviewed my plan of care/service agreement. I agree to the services that will be rendered and have no further questions. I have been informed what to do in an emergency/natural disaster. I have been informed verbally and in writing regarding the Agency policy on hazardous waste disposal in the home. I have been advised verbally and in writing the purpose and my rights pertaining to the collection of OASIS information and the OASIS Privacy Act. I have received the HIPAA/Notice of Privacy Practices and consent to the Agency's use and/or disclosure of protected health information for payment, treatment and the Agency's Health care operations." }, { key: "photograph", title: "Photographs and video of their care", pages: "10", group: "permissions", say: "Permission to photograph or film while we care for them, used for treatment purposes only.", watchFor: "The packet says outright they may refuse and it will not affect their care or payment. Say that before asking. They also get no payment for it, and can stop the filming at any time.", mark: "signature", mandatory: false, allowNotApplicable: true, fullText: 'CONSENT TO PHOTOGRAPH. I hereby consent to be photographed while receiving care from Joy Healthcare. The term "photograph" includes video or still photography, in digital or any other format, and any other means of recording or reproducing images. I hereby authorize the use of the photograph(s) by, or disclosure of the photograph(s) to: Joy Healthcare Services, 2700 Post Oak Blvd. Ofc 22-151, Galleria Office Tower 1, Houston, TX 77056-5784. PURPOSE: I hereby authorize the use or disclosure of the photograph(s) for treatment purposes. EXPIRATION: The Authorization expires at the end of rendered services or by written revocation of termination. Upon expiration of this Authorization, Joy Healthcare will not permit further release of any photograph(s), and will not be able to call back any photographs or information already released. MY RIGHTS: I may request cessation of filming or recording at any time. I may rescind this Authorization up until a reasonable time before the photograph is used, but I must do so in writing and submit it to the address listed above. I may inspect or obtain a copy of any photograph whose use or disclosure I am authorizing. I may refuse to sign this Authorization. My refusal will not affect my ability to obtain treatment or payment or eligibility. I have a right to receive a copy of this Authorization. I understand that I will not receive any financial compensation.' }, { key: "transportation", title: "Driving them places", pages: "11", group: "permissions", say: "Whether a caregiver may drive them \u2014 appointments, errands, social outings \u2014 in the caregiver's own car.", watchFor: "Say the insurance sentence out loud. Joy carries no commercial auto cover, and the caregiver's personal policy is what applies. Mileage is billed separately at $0.70 a mile, plus parking and tolls.", mark: "signature", mandatory: false, allowNotApplicable: true, fullText: 'NON-MEDICAL TRANSPORTATION CONSENT & AGREEMENT. At Joy Health, we are committed to providing safe, supportive, and seamless care experiences, including transportation as part of our concierge-level services. I authorize Joy Healthcare Services, LLC ("Joy Health") to provide non-medical transportation for the above named patient. SCOPE OF TRANSPORTATION: Transportation may include medical appointments, errands, and social outings as agreed upon within the care plan. CAREGIVER USE OF VEHICLE: Transportation is provided by a caregiver using a personal vehicle. Caregivers are not licensed medical transport providers. INSURANCE & LIABILITY: All caregivers maintain personal auto insurance in accordance with Texas state requirements. Joy Health does not provide commercial auto insurance coverage for caregiver vehicles and is not responsible for incidents, delays, or accidents that may occur during transport, except in cases of gross negligence. CLIENT RESPONSIBILITIES: The client agrees to be ready at the scheduled time, wear a seatbelt at all times, and follow all safety guidance provided by the caregiver. SAFETY CONDITIONS: Services may be adjusted, delayed, or declined if conditions are deemed unsafe, including but not limited to weather, environment, or changes in client condition. MILEAGE & FEES: Mileage may be billed separately at a rate determined by Joy Health ($0.70 per mile). Additional expenses such as parking or tolls may apply. ACKNOWLEDGMENT & CONSENT: By signing below, I acknowledge and accept the terms of this agreement and consent to transportation services provided.' }, { key: "disclose_medical_records", title: "Letting other providers send us their records", pages: "12", group: "records", say: "Permission for their doctors, hospitals, labs and pharmacy to send us what they hold, so we are not working blind.", watchFor: "Valid one year from signature, and revocable in writing at any time.", mark: "signature", mandatory: false, allowNotApplicable: true, fullText: "AUTHORIZATION TO DISCLOSE MEDICAL RECORDS. I authorize any health care provider including, but not limited to, any health care professional, hospital, clinic, laboratory, pharmacy or other medically related facility or service that has information about my health to disclose any and all of this information to Joy Healthcare Services, LLC and its duly authorized representatives. Information about my health may relate to any disorder of the immune system including, but not limited to, HIV and AIDS; use of drugs and alcohol; and mental and physical history, condition, advice or treatment, but does not include psychotherapy notes. I understand any information Joy Healthcare obtains pursuant to this authorization will be used for home care services. I further understand that the information is subject to re-disclosure and might not be protected by certain federal regulations governing the privacy of health information. This authorization is valid for one (1) year from the date below. A photographic or electronic copy of this authorization is as valid as the original. I understand I am entitled to receive a copy of this authorization. I may revoke this authorization in writing at any time except to the extent Joy Healthcare has relied on the authorization prior to notice of revocation. I understand if I revoke, alter, or do not sign this authorization, Joy Healthcare may not be able to provide the services described above. I understand this authorization will remain in effect until I revoke it in writing." }, { key: "obtain_release_medical_records", title: "Sending their records out to someone else", pages: "13", group: "records", say: "The other direction: who we may send records to, which records, and covering what dates.", watchFor: "Do not leave the record types or the date range blank. This one expires twelve months from signature, not at end of service.", mark: "signature", mandatory: false, allowNotApplicable: true, fullText: "AUTHORIZATION TO OBTAIN & RELEASE MEDICAL RECORDS. I hereby authorize the named provider to disclose the health records of the named individual. I am requesting that the Provider copy the following records and send the records to the named requester. DATES OF DISCLOSURE: from the beginning date to the end date stated. Records will be used for the purpose to render care/services. INFORMATION TO BE DISCLOSED: All Medical Records; Medication List; Discharge Summary; Office/Progress Notes; Hospitalization Records; Labs/Radiology Reports; other pertinent information. I understand I have the right to inspect and/or request a copy of the information to be disclosed and I may withdraw this authorization in writing at any time, except to the extent that action has been taken based on this authorization. I understand this authorization shall expire, without my expressed revocation, twelve (12) months from the date of signature. I am aware that once this information has been disclosed per my instructions, the information is subject to re-disclosure and may no longer be protected by the Federal Privacy Law of 1996 (HIPAA). If the patient is unable to sign, please indicate such and the authority to act of the person who is signing for the patient. The agency/facility, its employees, officers, and physicians are hereby released from any legal responsibility or liability for disclosure of the above information to the extent indicated and authorized herein." }, { key: "disclosure_list", title: "Who we are allowed to talk to about them", pages: "14", group: "records", say: "The names of the people we may discuss their care with. Up to four. Everyone else gets nothing, including family.", watchFor: "Get the relationship and a phone number for each, not just a first name. If they name nobody, that is a valid answer and the office needs to know it \u2014 we will not be able to update a daughter who calls.", mark: "signature", mandatory: false, allowNotApplicable: true, fullText: "HEALTH INFORMATION AUTHORIZED DISCLOSURE LIST. The patient or the authorized patient representative has given Joy Healthcare permission to disclose the patient's protected health information to the following individuals (up to four, each with name, relationship, phone, address and city/state/zip)." }, { key: "hipaa_privacy", title: "The privacy notice", pages: "15", group: "records", say: "How their health information may be used and disclosed, and how they can see it. They keep a copy.", watchFor: "The Privacy Officer's number is the office line, 713 231 9662 \u2014 this packet prints it correctly, unlike the old one. They may ask us to restrict how their information is used; we weigh those requests and are not obliged to agree.", mark: "initials", mandatory: true, fullText: "HIPAA PRIVACY RULE RECEIPT OF INFORMATION PRIVACY PRACTICES. Consent For The Use And Disclosure Of Protected Health Information For Treatment, Payment, Or Health Care Options. I understand that as part of my continued health care, Joy Healthcare, and its affiliated companies create and maintain health records containing information about my individual health history, symptoms, examination, and test results, diagnosis and treatments provided to me, future treatment plans and payment for care provided to me. I understand that this information serves as: a record indicating my care and treatment; a communication instrument among the many health professionals who contribute to my care; a history of diagnosis and treatment information utilized in the billing process; a verification source available to Medicare and Medicaid to review against billed and provided services; an assessment tool defining quality and reviewing competence of health care professionals. I understand that I have the right to request restrictions as to how my health information may be used or disclosed to carry out treatment, payment or health care operations, that Joy Healthcare will weigh those requests and abide with all mutually agreed upon restrictions. Joy Healthcare is not required to agree to the restrictions requested. NOTICE OF PRIVACY PRACTICES: This notice describes how medical information about you may be used and disclosed and how you can obtain access to this information. If you have any questions about this Notice of Privacy Practices, please contact our Privacy Officer: Karynn Verrett RN, BSN, CCM at 713 231 9662. We are required to abide by the terms of this Notice of Privacy Practices. We may change the terms of our notice at any time; the new notice will be effective for all protected health information maintained at that time. Upon your request, the facility will provide you with any revised Notice of Privacy Practices. Your protected health information may be used and disclosed by Joy Healthcare, the office staff, and others outside the office who are involved in your care and treatment, to pay your medical care bills, and to support the operation of Joy Healthcare." }, { key: "bill_of_rights", title: "The patient's bill of rights", pages: "16, 17", group: "rights", say: "Their rights: dignity, privacy, knowing what care costs before it starts, refusing care, and changing caregiver without any fear of reprisal.", watchFor: "The right to request a different caregiver without reprisal is the one clients most need to hear said out loud. So is the 30-day rule: we must tell them in writing within 30 days if what they owe changes.", mark: "initials", mandatory: true, fullText: "PATIENT'S BILL OF RIGHTS. The patient has the right to be informed of his or her rights. Joy Healthcare must protect and promote the exercise of these rights, and must provide the patient with written notice of the patient's rights in advance of furnishing care or during the initial evaluation visit before the initiation of treatment. Consistent with state laws, the patient's family or guardian may exercise the patient's rights when the patient is unable to do so. PATIENTS AND FAMILIES HAVE THE RIGHT: to have his or her property treated with respect, courtesy, and consideration; to be free from mental and physical abuse and property exploitation; to be assured that home health/care employees are prohibited from accepting gifts or borrowing from patients and caregivers; to have relationships with home health/care organizations that are based on honesty and ethical standards of conduct; to voice grievances and complaints related to home health/care services or care that is, or fails to be, furnished. FINANCIAL: to be advised, before care is initiated, of the extent to which payment may be required from the patient; to be advised orally and in writing of any changes in that liability as soon as possible, but no later than 30 calendar days from the date the agency becomes aware of a change; to have access, upon request, to all bills for services received. DECISION MAKING: to information regarding diagnosis, prognosis, and change in either; to participate in the planning of his or her care; to refuse services and to be advised of the consequences of refusing care; to be informed of any change in the plan of care before the change is made; to request a change in caregiver without fear of reprisal or discrimination; to receive written information, in advance, concerning policies on advance directives." }, { key: "complaints_policy", title: "The complaints policy", pages: "18", group: "rights", say: "How to complain, to us and to the state, and that complaining changes nothing about their care.", watchFor: "Read the state hotline number out rather than pointing at it. A family that has to go looking for it is a family that has already decided we would not help.", mark: "initials", mandatory: true, fullText: "COMPLAINTS POLICY. Our commitment to quality of care and a positive experience for your family remains our team's primary goal. Please feel free to call Joy Healthcare with any complaints or concerns: 713 231 9662. A staff member is available 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. Clients may voice complaints or concerns without fear of discrimination, retaliation, or interruption of appropriate services. Joy Healthcare Services, LLC will review and address complaints in accordance with agency policy and Texas requirements. For complaints or questions regarding home care/PAS services: Texas Health and Human Services Commission, Complaint and Incident Intake, Mail Code E249, P.O. Box 149030, Austin, Texas 78714-9030. Toll free 1-800-458-9858, open 7AM-7PM Monday to Friday. ciicomplaints@hhs.texas.gov." }, { key: "self_determination", title: "The Patient Self Determination Act", pages: "19", group: "rights", say: "Their right to make their own healthcare decisions, and that nobody can require an advance directive as a condition of getting care.", watchFor: "The sentence that matters is the one about compulsion: it is unlawful to require an advance directive before providing services. Families sometimes arrive believing the opposite.", mark: "initials", mandatory: true, fullText: "PATIENT SELF DETERMINATION ACT. The United States government and most individual state governments have enacted laws that protect the rights of adult individuals to make decisions concerning their own health care. These rights include the right to accept or refuse medical or surgical treatment and the right to formulate an advance directive as permitted under state law. An advance directive is a living will, a durable power of attorney for health care, and/or another written document that is executed by the individual, signed, dated, and expresses the individual's health care treatment decisions; it provides a way for the individual to state his or her wishes regarding his or her own health care decisions should the individual become incapacitated. Under these laws, it is unlawful for any person or organization to require an individual to execute an advance directive as a condition for receiving services or care." }, { key: "direct_employment", title: "The non-solicitation agreement", pages: "20", group: "rights", say: "They agree not to employ our staff directly, during care and for six months after the agreement ends.", watchFor: "The fee is not nominal: 26 weeks at 40 hours a week at the hourly rate. Say the six months out loud \u2014 families think it ends when care ends. It does not.", mark: "initials", mandatory: true, fullText: "DIRECT EMPLOYMENT OF AGENCY STAFF: I understand and agree to respect the rights of Joy Healthcare Services, LLC. and will not directly employ any staff provided by Joy Healthcare Services, LLC. for current client(s) or for other family members needing service. Once the agreement has been fulfilled between Joy Health and client, staff are not allowed to work with a previous client or family member directly through other channels for 6 months, unless through our agency. If the undersigned is found altering the terms of this clause the undersigned agrees to pay a liquidation fee equal to (26) weeks of service at (40) hours a week, at costs of the hourly price." }, { key: "disaster_plan", title: "The emergency preparedness plan", pages: "25", group: "rights", say: "What happens in a hurricane or an evacuation \u2014 the level of help they would need, who would come, and how they would travel.", watchFor: "The line families most often assume the opposite of: Joy does not evacuate or transport anybody. Say it plainly, and offer STEAR \u2014 the state registry is how the county knows to check on somebody who cannot leave.", mark: "signature", mandatory: true, fullText: "EMERGENCY PREPAREDNESS PLAN. At-risk home health or homecare patient criteria. Level 1 - Independent: client can safely evacuate or shelter and arrange transportation independently. Level 2 - Assistance Needed: client needs assistance but has reliable family, caregiver, or other support available. Level 3 - High Priority: client cannot safely evacuate independently and/or does not have reliable support or transportation. The plan records an emergency support person and phone, whether transportation is available, whether special transportation is needed, and the client's status on the State of Texas Emergency Assistance Registry (STEAR): registered, offered assistance and declined, or not applicable. Client/responsible party will coordinate evacuation and transportation with family, emergency contacts, or community resources. The agency will communicate regarding continuity of services when feasible during an emergency. I acknowledge that my Emergency Preparedness Plan has been reviewed with a Joy Health representative and is current and accurate to the best of my knowledge. I understand and agree with the plan outlined above and will notify Joy Health of any changes that may affect my emergency needs or support. I understand that Joy Health is not responsible for physically evacuating or transporting me during an emergency. Evacuation and transportation arrangements remain the responsibility of the client/responsible party, family, emergency contacts, or appropriate community/emergency resources." }];
